          "homepage": "",
          "overview": "In 1911, Mongolia stands at a historic turning point. After more than two centuries of Manchu foreign rule under the Qing Dynasty, a secret resistance forms to reclaim a free and sovereign nation. At the forefront of this dangerous movement are the visionary Bogd Khan and the determined minister Namnansuren. Navigating diplomatic negotiations with Russia and building an underground intelligence network, the insurgents must break through a web of espionage and political intrigue. As the situation escalates, a armed conflict erupts, forcing the rebels to pay with bloody sacrifices to secure the dream of freedom and protect a sacred prophecy.",
